    "post_commit": [
      {
        "mode": "business_logic",
        "business_logic": {
          "method": "create_payment_process_record",
          "description": "Insert a payment process record for the submitted expense",
          "spec": "Fires after commit of this transaction (Manage Approval, header form EXPTRACK_EXPENSE, action 'Submit' / system_op 'save'). If the payload's action/txn context is not a save of the header form via the Submit action, return without doing anything. Otherwise, using the header values from the just-submitted EXPTRACK_EXPENSE record, INSERT one new row into EXPTRACK_PAYMENT_PROCESS populated ONLY from the real submitted record's own column values (never sample, random, fetched, or imported data): EXPENSE_ID = header EXPENSE_ID; EMPLOYEE = header EMPLOYEE; CATEGORY = header CATEGORY; EXPENSE_DATE = header EXPENSE_DATE; PAYMENT_METHOD = header PAYMENT_METHOD; STATUS = header STATUS; EXPENSE_REPORT = the EXPENSE_REPORT id column on the header EXPTRACK_EXPENSE row (the linked report); TRIP and TOTAL_AMOUNT = read from the EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT row identified by that EXPENSE_REPORT id (its TRIP and TOTAL_AMOUNT columns). This is a cleanup/side-effect insert only; do not block or roll back the save on failure, but log/report any error encountered."
        }
      },
      {
        "mode": "business_logic",
        "business_logic": {
          "method": "return_voucher_to_expense_report",
          "description": "Return a rejected voucher to the Expense Report transaction",
          "spec": "Fires after commit of this transaction (Manage Approval, header form EXPTRACK_EXPENSE, action 'Submit' / system_op 'save'). If the just-saved header EXPTRACK_EXPENSE.STATUS is not exactly 'Reject', return without doing anything. Otherwise check EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT_NEW for an existing row where EXPENSE_ID = the header's EXPENSE_ID. If a row already exists, UPDATE it (do not create a duplicate); if not, INSERT a new row. Populate the row using only the real submitted header EXTRACK_EXPENSE record's own column values (never sample, random, fetched, or imported data): RECORD_ID = auto_generate() on insert only; EXPENSE_ID = header EXPENSE_ID; EMPLOYEE = header EMPLOYEE; CATEGORY = header CATEGORY; EXPENSE_DATE = header EXPENSE_DATE; PAYMENT_METHOD = header PAYMENT_METHOD; APPROVER_NAME = header APPROVER; RECEIPT_ATTACHMENT = header RECEIPT_ATTACHMENT; TRIP = look up EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT.TRIP where EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT.REPORT_ID = the header's EXPENSE_REPORT column value; TRIP_NAME = look up EXPTRACK_TRIP.TRIP_NAME where EXPTRACK_TRIP.TRIP_ID = that TRIP value. If the header's EXPENSE_REPORT is null/blank, still upsert the row but leave TRIP and TRIP_NAME blank. This returns the voucher to the Expense Report screen (exptrack_expense_report_new / table EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT_NEW), where the employee can Edit it for correction (that screen has no Add action \u2014 records only appear here via this hand-off). This is a side-effect upsert only; do not block or roll back the Manage Approval save on failure, but log/report any error encountered. Also set TOTAL_AMOUNT on the upserted EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT_NEW row by looking up EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT.TOTAL_AMOUNT where EXPTRACK_EXPENSE_REPORT.REPORT_ID = the header EXPTRACK_EXPENSE record's EXPENSE_REPORT column value (the same lookup already used for TRIP/TRIP_NAME); if the header's EXPENSE_REPORT is null/blank, leave TOTAL_AMOUNT blank as well."
        }
      }
    ],
